{
  "sourceId": "thinksr",
  "title": "ThinkSR: compact thought, dense output",
  "lang": "en",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s01-flow",
      "intent": "The recurrence returns to the DQ-CTM thought stage, while the overall image flow stays encoder to decoder.",
      "claim": "ThinkSR end to end: encoder, windows, shared DQ-CTM ticks, decoder.",
      "narration": "The image first becomes a dense carrier, because super-resolution needs spatial detail. Windowing organizes that carrier before the thought process reads it. The compact thought process ticks repeatedly on the windowed carrier. The loop returns only to that thought stage, not to the whole pipeline. The same DQ-CTM parameters are reused across ticks before decoding produces the output.",
