    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The equation first creates a dense feature field from the low-resolution image, then partitions that field into tokens without discarding them.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into the dense feature field. The feature field is the carrier that the compact thought process can read and update. The window operator partitions that carrier into token windows. The equation keeps the field inside the token set instead of replacing it with a single thought vector.",
